# shadcn/ui Components

This project uses **shadcn/ui** for all UI elements. Never build UI components from scratch when a shadcn/ui component exists.

## Setup

shadcn/ui is already initialised. Components live in `src/components/ui/`.

## Adding Components

If a component is not yet installed, run:

```bash
npx shadcn@latest add <component-name>
```

Examples:
```bash
npx shadcn@latest add button
npx shadcn@latest add card
npx shadcn@latest add input
npx shadcn@latest add dialog
```

## Usage

Import from the `@/components/ui` alias:

```tsx
import { Button } from "@/components/ui/button"
import { Card, CardContent, CardHeader, CardTitle } from "@/components/ui/card"
```

## Rules

- Always prefer shadcn/ui components over custom-built alternatives
- Use the `cn()` utility from `@/lib/utils` for conditional class merging
- Do not modify files inside `src/components/ui/` directly — extend via wrapper components instead
